There are three versions of the editor :	sedtvt100	resets the terminal to vt100 mode on exit	sedtvt220	resets the terminal to vt220 mode on exit	sedtvtxxx	resets the terminal to vt100 or vt220 mode 			depending on the TERM environment variable.			It also calls the shell given in SHELL for			':sys' calls rather than the standard shell.The sources for the vt100 version are includedLoad the editor you wish to /dd/cmds/e and the three files given inthe sys directory and then away you go!